1
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,940
[Sung Inho]

2
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,480
[Kim Domin]

3
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:50,100
[Summertime]

4
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:00,780
It's so delicious.

5
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:02,270
Thank you.

6
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:05,379
Hello.

7
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:06,350
Welcome.

8
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:07,020
Hello.

9
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:08,390
Two servings of pork belly,

10
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:10,620
one soybean paste stew,
and one bottle of soju, right?

11
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,080
Yes, I will leave it to you.

12
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,020
Thank you.

13
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:14,390
Just give me a moment.

14
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,890
Drop the honorifics.

15
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:22,780
You don't have to turn your head to drink.
Just drink it like that.

16
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:31,330
[New Message]
[To: Yeo Eunho: Eunho, I...]

17
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:40,490
Here's the alcohol.

18
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:41,360
Thank you.

19
00:01:41,479 --> 00:01:42,460
Enjoy your meal.

20
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,680
Do you need a receipt?

21
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,280
It's okay.

22
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,020
Okay.

23
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:48,200
Thank you.

24
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:49,420
Take some candy.

25
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:50,310
Thank you.

26
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:51,710
Take care.

27
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,960
[Yeo Eunho]

28
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,150
[Cha Dohyun: good at studying, student council president,
handsome, can get into a good school, can find a good job]

29
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:42,290
[Me: bad at studying, a proud member of the school,
handsome and cute, can work at my parents, live with Cha Dohyun]

30
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:44,070
[Childhood friends? Old friends? Lovers?]
[All of the above]

31
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:50,370
You are the only one I like.

32
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,650
You like a lot of things,

33
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:56,050
and you are very capable.

34
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:59,320
Whether it's back in school or now,

35
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,220
when I'm with you,

36
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,660
I'm always the worse off one.

37
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:03,930
Just find someone as good as you.

38
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,890
Thank you for the meal, sir.

39
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:17,990
Thank you. Take care.

40
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:19,850
-Take care.
-Thank you.

41
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:26,150
Gosh, sir, can we close now?

42
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:27,890
Okay, let's close.

43
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:29,000
Eunho,

44
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,900
let us know whenever
you've made up your mind.

45
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,900
This barbecue restaurant is yours.

46
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:33,910
Okay.

47
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:35,600
By the way, Eunho,

48
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,050
a part-timer is coming tomorrow.

49
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:39,980
A part-timer?

50
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,530
Who is it?

51
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,820
Hello.

52
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,150
Please take care of me.

53
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,829
My back has been hurting lately.

54
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:55,490
My knees hurt too.

55
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,360
He'll only work for a month.

56
00:03:58,930 --> 00:04:00,190
A month?

57
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,020
I'll leave him to you.

58
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,060
Yes, Professor.

59
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:14,820
I have something to do today,

60
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,019
so I can't attend the dinner.

61
00:04:17,930 --> 00:04:19,200
I'm sorry.

62
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:25,830
Just go.

63
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:27,810
That dinner must be very important to you.

64
00:04:27,810 --> 00:04:29,760
I'll handle my own business.

65
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,210
I'm here to work part-time.

66
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,470
Put on the apron.

67
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,290
After the customer orders,
enter the table number first.

68
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,909
There are 5 side dishes.

69
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:53,740
The cabbage salad will wilt
if mixed in advance,

70
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,860
so it must be mixed right before serving.

71
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:58,100
When cutting meat, cut against the grain
so it's tender.

72
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,250
You should serve the alcohol to the table

73
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,880
instead of letting the customers
get it themselves.

74
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,160
When changing the grill pan,
to prevent oil splatters,

75
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,000
don't forget to cover it with the new pan
before taking it out.

76
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,940
Right—

77
00:05:05,650 --> 00:05:07,600
clean the table immediately
after the customer leaves.

78
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,670
Make sure it's clean
before seating the next customer.

79
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,800
Understood?

80
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,790
This cabbage salad looks stale.

81
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:49,420
Toss it gently so it won't wilt.

82
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,240
You got my clothes dirty.

83
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,260
I'm sorry.

84
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:35,940
What are you staring at?
Get back to work.

85
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:38,200
Oh.

86
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:54,810
Today is your last day, right?

87
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,870
Good job this past month.

88
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,110
Your salary has been transferred.

89
00:07:08,150 --> 00:07:10,080
Yeo Eunho, I have something to say.

90
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:19,720
Is there anything left to say between us?

91
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:25,050
I'm off.

92
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,090
Whether in the past or now,

93
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:47,120
you're still so selfish.

94
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:54,190
Let's break up, Yeo Eunho.

95
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,740
Cha Dohyun. Cha Dohyun!

96
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,190
Cha Dohyun!

97
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,640
You called out to Dohyun so anxiously,

98
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,630
as if you were breaking up.

99
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:45,760
I don't know. I had a nightmare.

100
00:08:46,770 --> 00:08:49,370
Have you taught him everything
about the shop?

101
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:52,720
He won't be coming anymore anyway.

102
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:00,070
According to solar terms,

103
00:09:00,210 --> 00:09:02,500
we've officially crossed the threshold
into summer.

104
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,580
It'll be mostly sunny
across the country today,

105
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,000
with daytime temperatures soaring

106
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:06,790
and bringing blistering heat everywhere.

107
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:08,520
By the way, did Dohyun tell you?

108
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:09,800
As temperatures rise sharply...

109
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,800
He said he's going to Vietnam next week
to help with Jihyun's business.

110
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,000
there will be

111
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,260
no major rainfall expected
for the foreseeable future.

112
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:17,570
Fair and dry conditions will persist.

113
00:09:17,570 --> 00:09:20,030
It seems he's going to stay
and not come back.

114
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:22,760
He's going to stay?

115
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:23,710
Yeah.

116
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:26,840
Jihyun's business is growing.

117
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,780
After all,
it's good for the family to be together.

118
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,430
Yeo Eunho, I have something to say.

119
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:53,810
[Cha Dohyun]

120
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:02,320
Yeo Eunho, come out.

121
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:07,190
I'm dying of heat. Come out immediately.

122
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:13,360
Where are you going? Aren't you eating?

123
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,260
Yeo Eunho.

124
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,550
I'm doomed.

125
00:11:18,710 --> 00:11:21,260
I thought a lot when you weren't around.

126
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:24,320
The conclusion is no.

127
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:33,120
I thought a hundred times—

128
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,860
no, a thousand times—

129
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:38,950
I can't live without you.

130
00:11:43,850 --> 00:11:45,980
That thing you said about breaking up,

131
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,830
take it back.

132
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:50,980
I'll pretend I never heard it.

133
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:58,750
I never thought you weren't good enough
for me.

134
00:11:58,750 --> 00:12:00,940
Nor did I think I was out of your league.

135
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,630
Because you are the standard,

136
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:08,480
there is no other standard
to measure against.

137
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:10,510
So,

138
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:13,510
just be yourself.

139
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,270
No matter what you look like

140
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:21,300
or what you do,

141
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:26,110
let me be the one to like you.

142
00:12:46,770 --> 00:12:48,950
Don't ever say things like that again.

143
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:52,660
Never.

144
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:40,220
Mom, I'm taking the day off today.

145
00:13:41,290 --> 00:13:42,140
Hey!

146
00:13:42,310 --> 00:13:44,620
Where are you going instead of working?

147
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,970
Hey, Eunho,
we have a group of customers today!

148
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,750
Oh my god, he's exactly my type.

149
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:00,490
Where?

150
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,480
Hey, don't stare so obviously.

151
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,830
The guy sitting over there.

152
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,700
Could he be a sports major?

153
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:11,140
Why would a sports major sit in front
of the business administration building?

154
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:14,010
They have to take some
general education courses too, you know.

155
00:14:14,010 --> 00:14:17,010
But whether it's his looks or his body,
he's really...

156
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,250
Handsome, right?

157
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,930
If you look closely,
he's even more handsome.

158
00:14:22,010 --> 00:14:25,010
Eyes, nose, mouth.

159
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:29,340
He looks really handsome
when he just wakes up.

160
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,500
It's a pity that you won't get to see

161
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,050
his real face.

162
00:14:33,490 --> 00:14:36,120
Did you know he's also secretly muscular?

163
00:14:39,030 --> 00:14:40,390
Yeo Eunho.

164
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,890
What's going on?

165
00:14:53,070 --> 00:14:54,420
What did you say to them?

166
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,670
Something.

167
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:00,110
Let's go.

168
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,130
Hmm? Where are we going?

169
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,100
You'll see when we get there.

170
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,600
Where are we going?

171
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,420
Over there.

172
00:15:23,330 --> 00:15:25,910
Look, a lunchbox
made by Yeo Eunho himself.

173
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:34,260
What are you doing?

174
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:36,790
Because I like you.

175
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,360
Let's eat. I'm hungry.

176
00:15:45,930 --> 00:15:46,900
Say "ah."

177
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:55,550
Is it good?

178
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:58,530
Yeah, it's good.

179
00:16:00,410 --> 00:16:01,730
You have some too.

180
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,050
Have another one.

181
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:14,720
I'm done.

182
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:15,840
Just one last bite.

183
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:16,760
No.

184
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:18,780
Is it good?

185
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,570
Hey, you have some too.

186
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,610
Eat up.

187
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:27,410
Have another one.

188
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:29,990
Say "ah"—

189
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,370
"ah."

190
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:03,370
Cha Dohyun.

191
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:10,440
Fulfill a wish of mine.

192
00:17:11,869 --> 00:17:12,980
What is it?

193
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:16,380
Whatever I say next,

194
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:19,190
don't laugh and just repeat after me.

195
00:17:23,069 --> 00:17:24,260
I love you.

196
00:17:32,390 --> 00:17:33,530
I love you more.

197
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,300
What's going on?

198
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,760
What do you mean?

199
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:29,310
It's break time now.

200
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:38,210
But why are you wearing a school uniform?

201
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:43,530
Students should wear school uniforms.
What else would I wear?

202
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:49,230
Are you still half asleep?

203
00:19:00,170 --> 00:19:01,330
So it was a dream.

204
00:19:11,670 --> 00:19:12,690
Cha Dohyun.

205
00:19:13,670 --> 00:19:15,730
What are you going to do after school?

206
00:19:17,610 --> 00:19:19,270
What do you want to do?

207
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,900
Wanna go to an internet cafe
and play games?

208
00:19:26,090 --> 00:19:27,190
Sure.

209
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:30,190
Actually, no.

210
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:33,580
Let's just go home
and have instant noodles.

211
00:19:34,470 --> 00:19:35,880
Sounds good.

212
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:47,690
You're acting weird today.

213
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:54,340
Cha Dohyun, what's the date today?

214
00:19:55,890 --> 00:19:56,920
What?

215
00:19:57,940 --> 00:20:00,040
Your birthday is coming up, right?

216
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,070
What are you doing?

217
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:35,350
Don't move. I'm going to give you a gift.

218
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,920
Here. That's your gift.

219
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:50,740
What is this?

220
00:20:52,550 --> 00:20:53,800
Proof.

221
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:55,710
What?

222
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,940
Proof that you're mine.

223
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:06,530
I don't know yet,

224
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:10,470
but you'll probably make me stressed a lot
in the future.

225
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:13,750
So I had to do something

226
00:21:14,150 --> 00:21:16,440
so I wouldn't feel so wronged.

227
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:21,740
You're the one who's still half asleep,

228
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,780
so why do I feel like
I'm the one dreaming?

229
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,810
That's the school bell.

230
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:37,370
Go back to your class, Cha Dohyun.

231
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,070
Where are you going?

232
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:42,980
I'm...

233
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:46,300
also going to find where I belong.

234
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:56,000
You're not going somewhere else, right?

235
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:11,200
Cha Dohyun, don't worry.

236
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:15,490
My final destination
can only be by your side.

237
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:27,340
Come and catch me.

238
00:22:28,630 --> 00:22:30,530
I will always wait for you.

239
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:36,240
In this never-ending

240
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,520
summer of ours.

241
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:47,700
[Thank you all
for your support for "Summertime"]

242
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:54,500
[Summertime]
